      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe as written.\n\n- **Daily total:** 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day. The usual maximum for metformin is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release, so this is about twice the limit.\n- **Single dose:** 1700 mg in one dose is also well above the usual maximum of 850 to 1000 mg per dose. A dose that high raises the risk of severe GI effects and lactic acidosis.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the max for immediate-release.\n- **1000 mg PO twice daily with meals.** This is 2,000 mg/day.\n- **500 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 1,500 mg/day.\n- **1700 mg total per day.** For example, 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it. If you do want 1700 mg three times daily, please confirm that and give a clinical reason. I'll add that to the order note, though I'd advise against it."
      }
