       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. 5,100 mg/day is about twice the maximum daily dose, and a 1700 mg single dose is also far above the usual maximum. You haven't given a clinical reason that would justify it. The main risk is metformin-associated lactic acidosis, and there's no evidence of added glycemic benefit above about 2,000 to 2,550 mg/day.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day)\n- 1000 mg PO twice daily with meals (2,000 mg/day)\n- A lower starting dose, such as 500 mg PO twice daily with meals, titrated up\n\nIf you think a dose outside the labeled range is needed, please discuss it with the pharmacy or an attending and place it through your institution's override process. I can also enter the order if the dose was a typo or if you give me a different intended dose."
